          <h4>Rong Vang Hoang Gia</h4>
          <div class="work-modal__columns">
            <p>Officially registered for production and consumption in 1997, Hoang Giang Joint Stock Company has spent over two decades remaining steadfast on the path of preserving and developing Vietnamese traditional crafts. Mung bean cake has always stood as a profound cultural specialty of the Red River Delta.<br /><br />By selecting high-quality, meticulously standard input materials combined with advanced hygiene processes, the brand writes a story of cultural continuity, connecting the architectural identity and decades of expert experience to honor a national delicacy on an international scale.</p>
            <p>This project focuses entirely on a unique Mid-Autumn Festival edition, leaving the core brand identity and original Royal Golden Dragon logo completely untouched. The iconic circular emblem with its powerful dragon silhouette remains proudly at the center of the design to preserve brand authenticity and historical trust. By housing the timeless product in a fresh, festive jacket, the campaign aims to inject modern visual energy into the brand’s steady revenue stream, turning a familiar staple into a premium, desirable gift choice.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rvhg-logo"><img src={work4Logo} alt="Rong Vang Hoang Gia characters" /></div>
            <h4>“The Moon of Hope — The Moments of Longing”</h4>
            <div class="work-modal__columns">
            <p>The creative direction for this Mid-Autumn edition centers around a minimalist 2D flat illustration of the traditional Lion Dance. The graphic layout softens the formal look of the product into a playful, emotionally engaging experience that appeals directly to modern families and children.<br /><br />To pair beautifully with the original logo, we curated a custom typographic layout using L'Hanoienne typeface which expertly mirrors the nostalgic charm of classic Vietnamese signage while maintaining a clean appearance.</p>
            <p>The physical execution reinvents the unboxing ritual through an interactive, puzzle-like sliding box system. Moving away from ordinary commercial wrappers, the internal layout splits into modular components. The real magic happens when four individual boxes are stacked and aligned side-by-side: they puzzle together perfectly to reveal a single, cohesive lion artwork across the boxes. Accompanied by a premium matching carrier bag, this seasonal packaging effectively elevates structural safety into a festive, highly engaging interactive gift set.</p>
