        <section class="crescent-copy aanta-copy">
          <span class="crescent-copy__marker" aria-hidden="true" style="display: block; width: 31px; height: 31px; margin: 0 0 26px; background: var(--color-mint);"></span>
          <span class="crescent-copy__markers crescent-copy__markers--right" aria-hidden="true" style="display: flex; gap: 35px; position: absolute; top: 16px; right: clamp(1.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);"><span class="crescent-copy__marker" style="display: block; flex: 0 0 31px; width: 31px; height: 31px; background: var(--color-mint);"></span><span class="crescent-copy__marker" style="display: block; flex: 0 0 31px; width: 31px; height: 31px; background: var(--color-mint);"></span></span>
          <h4>Antibiotic Resistance</h4>
          <div class="work-modal__columns">
            <p>Nowadays, antibiotics are frequently used to treat infectious illnesses. Antibiotic misuse, on the other hand, can have negative consequences for patients, such as drug-specific side effects, and pose a public health risk due to the emergence of multidrug-resistant bacteria. As a result, novel antimicrobial therapeutic options are needed, focusing on medicines based on natural products.
                <br><br/>
                The overuse of antibiotics occurs due to the mistaken widespread belief that they are beneficial for a broad array of conditions and because many physicians are willing to prescribe antibiotics if patients ask for the medication.</p>
            <p>“Antibiotics Are Not the Answer” is a public awareness campaign addressing the growing issue of antibiotic misuse and resistance. The campaign aims to educate audiences about the dangers of self-medication and unnecessary antibiotic consumption.
                <br><br/>
                Through impactful visuals and clear messaging, the project encourages responsible healthcare decisions and promotes greater awareness of antimicrobial resistance. The creative approach focuses on transforming complex medical information into accessible and engaging visual communication.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="aanta-visuals">
            <div class="aanta-content-frame" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable campaign content preview"><img src={work5Content} alt="Antibiotics are not the answer campaign content" /></div>
            <div class="aanta-logo-column">
              <div class="aanta-logo"><img src={work5Logo} alt="Antibiotics are not the answer logo" /></div>
              <p class="aanta-copy__right">Overuse of antibiotics is both an individual and public health problem. Individuals who overuse antibiotics may be more vulnerable to antibiotic-related complications such as digestive problems, yeast infections, and allergic reactions. From a public health perspective, widespread antibiotic overuse allows bacteria to evolve resistance to antibiotics rapidly. This can create infections that do not respond to typical treatments.</p>
